      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Would really like to see this feature!\nIn my use cases, i do like to use a bit of immobile per default for IK movement. I also like the ability of having world immobile/joystick movement have more immobile and thus less impact on the movement. Currently, this is not possible.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-05T23:02:58.346Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The world mode for immobile is really good, but one really great improvement to see if possible, would be a blend multiplier between the two modes so you could actually control how much the Immobile value affects IK movement.\nFor example if you wanted IK movement to have 50% less of the Immobile value than the positional movement from the scene root, then you could set the blend to 0.5, however if you wanted it to act exactly how it does now with the most recent update [1194] you could set the blend to 0, and IK movement would have 0 of the Immobility value applied.",
